# Daily Digest — Agent & Cursor Rules

## Project type
Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, Supabase, Anthropic API.

## Component rules
- There are exactly 4 components: Header, PaperCard, ReadingView, TopicQueue
- Do NOT create new component files — add to existing ones or put logic in pages
- Pages (app/**) do the assembly and data fetching
- Server Components fetch data; Client Components handle interactivity

## Design tokens (never change these)
```
bg:         #f9f7f4
text:       #1a1a1a
border:     #e8e5e0
secondary:  #6b6b6b
card-bg:    #ffffff
font-serif: 'Playfair Display' (headings, pull quotes)
font-sans:  'Inter' (UI, body text, metadata)
```

## Design rules (never violate)
- NO drop shadows (`shadow-*`) on cards or any UI element
- NO border-radius on cards (`rounded-*` is banned on PaperCard)
- NO gradients anywhere
- Section labels are lowercase, followed by a full-width `border-t` rule
- "read more ›" links use `›` (›), not `>`

## Supabase
- Browser client: `lib/supabase.ts` → `createBrowserClient()`
- Server client: `lib/supabase.ts` → `createServerClient()` (uses service role in API routes)
- Never expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` to the browser

## API routes
- `/api/jobs/run-nightly` — protected by `Authorization: Bearer CRON_SECRET` header
- `/api/suggest-topics` — no auth, called from queue page client-side

## Anthropic
- Model: `claude-sonnet-4-6`
- Always use `web_search_20250305` tool for the nightly essay
- Essay output must be parsed as JSON: { title, subtitle, pull_quote, content, sources }

## Nightly job order
1. Verify CRON_SECRET
2. Pick top queued topic (priority desc, created_at asc)
3. Mark in_progress
4. generateEssay(topic)
5. Compute word_count, read_time_minutes
6. edition_number = MAX(edition_number) + 1
7. Insert paper, mark topic done
